From cb9cb979eed603f468846480a77c088aa7616b0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: erikfrish <erikfrish@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 17:36:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: support AmneziaWG 3.1 obfuscation parameters

A 3.1 server expects header protection, content padding and the
related timing ranges, none of which the plugin knew about, so a
client built from a 3.1 configuration never completed a handshake.

Add the nine new parameters across every layer: parsing and writing
in awg-config, storage and validation on AWGDevice, vpn.data
serialisation as connection-* keys, and encoding for both backends.
The external path writes them back into the generated awg-quick
configuration; the netlink path sends the 32-byte key, the u16
ranges packed as hi<<16 | lo to match the kernel u16_range_t, and
the u8 flags.

Ranges are validated with the same helper that encodes them, so a
value the kernel cannot represent is refused instead of being
dropped silently on the way out. The header protection key is
checked for the exact 32-byte length the kernel policy demands.

Signed-off-by: erikfrish <erikfrish@gmail.com>
